# PROD-22. Who answers for the parts of the repository where a mistake costs money, leaks data between
# stores or changes what reaches production. Today there is one maintainer, so every line has the same
# owner; the list is the useful part. When a second person joins, give them the areas they know here and
# turn on "Require review from Code Owners" in the main ruleset: until that setting is on, this file
# only marks who is asked for review, it does not block a merge.
#
# A pattern that matches nothing is ignored silently, so a renamed or moved path stops being protected
# without any error. Check them against `git ls-files` when a package moves.

# What gets built and shipped: workflows, dependency updates, build files, analysis and the committed
# environment template.
